  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protecting Livelihoods Assets through Anticipatory Actions in Flood Prone Communities in Northern Bangladesh (JAMUNA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is part of the Anticipatory Action framework for floods in Bangladesh and aims to protect the livelihoods and assets of vulnerable households before the anticipated flooding event. This project targets vulnerable communities in the districts of Bogra, Jamalpur, Gaibandha, Kurigram, and Sirajgani. This FAO project will provide highly nutritious animal feed to 11,310 vulnerable households. The project targets a total of 56,500 people, including 17,443 women, 17,174 men, 21,933 children, and 4,776 people with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
